#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY Data quality"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Checks at every tier; failing data is quarantined, never used."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-TRANSFORMATION]{1}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Keep bad data from consumers and keep it visible."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Data that fails its checks is worse than no data ([P10]{1}). Counting refusals apart from failures tells a bad source from a broken system."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Checks per tier; a quarantine with reasons; source contracts."
msgstr ""

