msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Each tier has checks, and data that fails a blocking check does not reach consumers; it is quarantined with a reason."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Inject a failing row; it appears in quarantine and not in gold."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Refused input and system failure are counted and reported separately."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Metrics distinguish the two; each has its own alert."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Each source has a declared contract (schema, keys, freshness) checked on arrival."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Change a source's schema in a test; arrival checks fail loudly."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Every check names the ISO/IEC 25012 data-quality characteristic it measures (for example accuracy, completeness, consistency, credibility or currentness) and its severity.{1}*Example:* The check 'enrolment date not before birth date' names the characteristic consistency and the severity blocking."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "The check registry has a dimension and severity for every check."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "An error found after load is fixed by a correction request approved by the data's steward; the correction lands as a new version, never an edit in place, and the request is kept with the record.{1}*Example:* An institution reported 120 learners in grade 4 instead of 210; the correction request records the new value, the reason 'transcription error', the scanned register as evidence and the steward's approval, and the census snapshot gets a new version."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "A correction fixture produces a new version linked to its request; the old version stays readable."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "CAP-QUALITY.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Checks that compare two sources which should agree are declared as blocking or warning."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-quality.md
msgid "Each cross-source check states its effect."
msgstr ""

